<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine cash soybeans slide after Chicago.</title>
<headline>Argentine cash soybeans slide after Chicago.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine cash soybeans slipped in the wake of a sharply lower Chicago midsession Wednesday, traders said.</p>
<p>FAS elevator soybeans lost $4 in Rosario to $280. But volume was very low, with many sellers hoping to ride out the lull. Sunflower seed prices were unchanged, with little supply. Maize prices were also steady, but there was little export demand.</p>
<p>(( -- Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
